    description: ""  # 04f9
    fields:  # 04f9
      statement: "'hypergumbo sketch --input behavior_map.json -t N --no-progress' must produce a sketch (or a clear error) for any N within the documented range. Currently every N >= 17000 reproducibly returns exit 141 (SIGPIPE) with stdout=0 bytes and stderr containing only a benign staleness note. Documented examples mention -t 16000 (last working value); -t 17000+ fails."  # 04f9
      root_cause: "Strace shows the main sketch process writes ~50KB of markdown to fd 4 (pipe to child subprocess), child exits cleanly (SIGCHLD si_status=0 si_utime=0.34s), parent's next write hits EPIPE 'Broken pipe' and is killed by SIGPIPE. The trigger is content volume above ~16k tokens. Independent of network (reproduces with HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1) — confirmed earlier HF safetensors_conversion crash is a separate symptom from a background thread. Whatever process reads fd 4 has a budget-sensitive exit condition that races against parent's write completion. Affects -t 17000 thru at least -t 64000 tested. Does NOT affect smaller -t budgets (500-16000 all work) or fresh-run on tiny repos."  # 04f9
- op: discuss  # fa34
  at: '2026-05-28T18:31:59Z'  # fa34
  by: agent  # fa34
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fa34
  clock: 2  # fa34
  nonce: fa34  # fa34
  message: "Pass-9 refinement: threshold narrowed via bisection to between 16100 and 16150 (NOT 17000). Repro: HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 hypergumbo /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo -t $N for N in 16000 16100 16150 16200 16250 16400-16800 17000 -> works at 16000/16100; exit 141 / 0 bytes at 16150+. The pass-8 estimate of 17000 was the original probe; the actual cliff is 16100-16150 (50-token window).\n\nPass-9 strace investigation (-e write,close,pipe,clone,execve -f, HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1, -t 17000):\n- Parent hypergumbo Python process (PID 309744) NEVER writes to fd 1 (stdout) or fd 2 (stderr).\n- The 8 writes captured to fd 1 are all from short-lived git child processes (git config --get remote.origin.url, git rev-list --max-parents=0 HEAD, git rev-parse, git status) — these are normal repo-identification calls that hypergumbo pipes from.\n- No SIGPIPE event captured in the strace.\n- No exit_group/exit syscall captured (trace was 1.4M lines of mostly close(3) cleanup).\n- Bash sees exit 141 (= 128 + SIGPIPE 13) but Python's actual death path is invisible to write/close/pipe/clone tracing.\n\nInterpretation: the failure happens INSIDE Python, not at a syscall boundary the strace flags cover. Likely candidates: a write to a non-stdio fd (e.g. internal pipe to embeddings model subprocess), Python signal handler firing during BytesIO buildup, or BrokenPipeError raised during embedding-stage pipe communication. Next probe: strace with -e trace=all to capture everything; or run sketch through 'python -X faulthandler' to dump the Python stack on signal.\n\nThe trace file was discarded because it captured a FORGEJO_TOKEN from a git remote URL — leaving the strace artifact in the workspace would violate the secrets policy."  # fa34
- op: discuss  # 36f7
  at: '2026-05-28T18:51:25Z'  # 36f7
  by: agent  # 36f7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 36f7
  clock: 3  # 36f7
  nonce: 36f7  # 36f7
  message: "Pass-10 refinement: with --debug, the LAST stderr line before death is '[hypergumbo_core.ranking] DEBUG: centrality: processing 29 files with 4701 patterns'. This is the second batch through _compute_centrality_with_python in ranking.py:1583. The function builds a single combined regex with 4701 alternatives (\\\\b(name1|name2|...|name4701)\\\\b) and runs it across files via ThreadPoolExecutor (max_workers=8).\n\nThe TT failure happens INSIDE this second batch. The faulthandler approach didn't help because: (a) running cli.main() in-process (via 'python -X faulthandler') still exited at 0 bytes stdout/stderr, suggesting sys.exit or signal occurs before faulthandler dumps; (b) -t 16150 with EVERY output mode (no redirect, > /dev/null, |cat > /dev/null, > file) produces exit 141 with 0 bytes. So the SIGPIPE-like exit is not from a downstream pipe close — it's from inside hypergumbo's own process.\n\nLikely candidates inside _compute_centrality_with_python:\n- ThreadPoolExecutor worker thread crashes (e.g., regex re.error on a problematic pattern, OSError on a bad file)\n- 4701-alternation regex causes catastrophic backtracking on a specific file content\n- futures.as_completed propagates an unhandled BrokenPipeError from inside a worker\n\nNext probe: instrument _compute_one to log per-file processing time / capture exceptions; or run with PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 to see which file is being processed when death occurs.\n\nSeverity remains HIGH — only command path affected is sketch (the most-used hypergumbo invocation). The bounce at 16150 (a token budget) suggests it's about which symbol set gets ranked, not the budget itself."  # 36f7
